From 7bfb2fb344c86b148b23ce2c52087f0fc03a4422 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: CipherScope <dev@cipherscope.io>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 08:33:14 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 40/48] consensus: activate OP_CHECKMLDSA44 at a height fixed
 for the Ark-0 signet

A buried deployment, p2mr_mldsa44, sets SCRIPT_VERIFY_P2MR_MLDSA44 on
blocks at or above its height where P2MR is active too.

The height is a rule of the network it applies to, so it is not an
option: two nodes of one signet could otherwise enforce different rules
under the same challenge, and split. It is ARK0_MLDSA44_HEIGHT, a
constant that applies only to the signet whose challenge is Ark-0's,
set to 8600 for the rollout of 2026-09-25. Any other signet, the default
signet, testnet3, testnet4 and mainnet never activate the rules.

Regtest activates at genesis unless -testactivationheight=p2mr_mldsa44@N
says otherwise. getdeploymentinfo reports the deployment, and a node
where it is enabled logs the height at startup.
